The project includes a monitoring dashboard designed for real-time visualization of the smart pintle control system.

The dashboard provides:

System status
Live clock
Target throttle control
Actual flow monitoring
Pintle position
Pressure monitoring
Differential pressure
Cavitation-risk indication
System health
Data logging
CSV export

The dashboard is initially designed to work with simulated data and can later be connected to physical hardware.

  Hardware-to-Dashboard Data Flow

The planned system architecture is:

  Physical Sensors
      ↓
ESP32 / Microcontroller
      ↓
Telemetry Data
      ↓
Firebase / Communication Layer
      ↓
Web Dashboard
      ↓
Real-Time Monitoring

  Simulation Mode

Before connecting physical hardware, the dashboard can operate in Simulation Mode.

Simulation Mode allows development and testing of:

Throttle commands
Flow response
Pintle position
Pressure variation
Risk indicators
Control logic
Data visualization

This reduces dependence on physical hardware during early software development.

  
